\f0\fs24 \cf0 Getting Bitwig to recognize the K-Board Pro 4 :\
\
1. Follow the instructions on the blue BitWig card that came with your K Board Pro 4 to download and authorize your copy of the software. \
\
2. When Bitwig was installed, it automatically created the folder 'Bitwig Studio' within your ~/Documents. Place the controller script (K-Board_Pro_4_control.js) in\
~/Documents/Bitwig Studio/Controller Scripts/\
\
3. Open Bitwig and go to the Dashboard (click on the small dots in top middle of the application).\
\
4. Go to the Settings tab (on top).\
\
5. Go to the Controllers tab (on the left).\
\
6. Click on the 'Add' button to the right of 'Controllers'. Select 'K-Board Pro 4' in the 'Keith McMillen' tab.\
(If your K-Board Pro 4 is already plugged in, Bitwig gives you a shortcut button to 'Add' the K-Board Pro 4 and you can skip step 8).\
\
7. The incoming and outgoing MIDI ports will be set to 'None'. Select K-Board Pro 4 Control Surface for each.\
\
       MIDI from the K-Board Pro 4 should now be coming into Bitwig Studio 8-Track! Try out our synth template to get some sounds going. \
\
\
\
Opening the Keith McMillen MPE synth template :\
\
1. We recommend placing the 'K-Board Pro 4 and QuNexus Bitwig Template' folder in\
~/Documents/Bitwig Studio/Projects\
\
2. Open this folder, and double click the 'K-Board Pro 4 and QuNexus  Bitwig Template.bwproject' file.\
\
3. Record enable one of the 8 demo synths by clicking the white circle to the right of the synth name, left of the 'S' button. \
\
       Enjoy! If you're not hearing anything, make sure your audio output is correctly selected. These settings are in the Dashboard, under Settings (top row), then Audio (on the left).}